<title>USA: BOTCC-CME sign letter of intent for common banking.</title>
<headline>BOTCC-CME sign letter of intent for common banking.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1996-09-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Chicago Mercantile Exchange (CME) and Board of Trade Clearing Corp (BOTCC) signed a letter of intent Wednesday to develop a common banking system, according to a copy of the letter obtained by Reuters.</p>
<p>CME and BOTCC, the clearing house for Chicago Board of Trade (CBOT), want to establish common banking and settlement procedures so that clearing members of both exchanges can use one account when doing business on either exchange.</p>
<p>The letter pegs a start-up date for common banking of August 1997.</p>
<p>--Chicago Derivatives Desk 312- 408-8750</p>
